  frame(dummyCtx, state);
  assert.ok(!brick.alive, 'Brick should be destroyed');
  assert.ok(state.ball.vy < 0, 'Ball should have bounced UP (vy < 0)');
});
```
Wait, the test calls `frame(dummyCtx, state)`. But I moved the collision logic to `step()`.
So `frame()` no longer destroys bricks or flips velocity.
The test fails because it doesn't call `step()`.

I should update my `D1` test in `game/neon.test.js` to call `step()` as well, or just use the logic that `Sonde` uses (which calls both).

Actually, I'll just update the test to be consistent with how the game works now.

